{"name":"Frosty Dawn","hex":"#cbe9c9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"frosty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cold, chilly; icy.","Having frost on it or in it."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frosty"},{"term":"dawn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To begin to brighten with daylight.","To start to appear or become obvious."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The morning twilight period immediately before sunrise.","The rising of the sun."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dawn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dawn","blocks":[{"text":"Dawn is the time that marks the beginning of twilight before sunrise. It is recognized by the appearance of indirect daylight being scattered in Earth's atmosphere, when the centre of the Sun's disc has reached 18° below the observer's horizon. This morning twilight period will last until sunrise, when direct daylight outshines the diffused light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Desert_Dawn.jpg/330px-Desert_Dawn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dawn","wikidata":"Q11326182"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg/500px-New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg/1280px-New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg/500px-New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dawn at La Silla Observatory, Chile[4]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANew_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Amanhecer_n